  "public": {
    "readme": "# Local smartlink integration\n\nWork directory: `/workspace`. Python 3.12.3 is preinstalled by shared python-web-services environment; use standard library only, no package downloads. CPU 2, RAM 2 GiB, process limit 256, temporary disk 512 MiB, network restricted to local prepared services. Build: `python -m compileall -q .`. The benchmark starts the prepared service on port 8090 before the task budget. For a standalone checkout, start it with `python local_service.py`. Health: `curl http://127.0.0.1:8090/health`. Public tests: `python /public_tests/smoke.py`. CLI: `python cli.py < example.json`. Reset: stop local service and restart; pass fresh state for each attempt. Prepared service log: `/tmp/smartlink-provider.log`; standalone service/CLI logs go to stderr. No external account is needed.\n\nImplement `process_smartlink_event(state,event,service=None)` plus `SmartlinkClient.authorize(code)` and `.send_conversion(platform,payload,key)`. Preserve input objects. State maps: smartlinks, oauth_states, spotify_users, clicks, streams, conversions. Attribution window is seconds (default 604800), supplied as a positive finite number. Events: oauth_start(user_id,state_token), oauth_complete(state_token,code), click(click_id,smartlink_id,destination,timestamp), stream(stream_id,click_id,user_id,timestamp), conversion(event_id,platform,stream_id), status(). IDs are nonempty strings; timestamps are seconds. Errors are `error.code`, successes are `result`; successful operations clear prior errors. The CLI processes events sequentially and prints final state. Existing status and OAuth initiation must remain working.\n\nAuthorization rejects absent, mismatched or consumed state and non-string/blank code before network access. Use form POST grant_type=authorization_code, code, redirect_uri with HTTP Basic authentication, then GET profile using Bearer access token. Authorize and consume state only after profile has a nonempty id. Store authorized and provider_user_id under the local spotify_users entry. Failures use authorization_failed; invalid callbacks use invalid_oauth_callback. Never put raw codes, secrets or access tokens into returned state. Additional click, stream, conversion and retry decisions are available from the synthetic client.\n\nConfiguration fields: token_url, profile_url, client_id, client_secret, redirect_uri, conversion_urls mapping. Local endpoints: `/token`, `/me`, `/meta`, `/tiktok` on http://127.0.0.1:8090. Development-only credentials: local-client / local-secret, code local-code, redirect_uri http://127.0.0.1:8090/callback. These are fabricated fixtures. Real credentials remain in client configuration only. The response from authorize is a profile dict; send_conversion returns decoded connector JSON. HTTP timeout must be bounded. Stream observations are trusted synthetic input, not live listening verification. This is a component extension; web UI, production traffic, vendor-native advertising APIs and live provider integration are outside scope.",
